<resources>
    <string name="onboarding_title_1">Ride with an extra layer of awareness</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_1">VahakVigil monitors supported phone motion sensors during a ride and can guide you through an emergency response when a possible incident is detected.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_2">Signals help identify possible incidents</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_2">Accelerometer and gyroscope readings are evaluated together. Detection is not guaranteed and can be affected by device placement, hardware, permissions and conditions.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_3">You can cancel the emergency countdown</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_3">When a possible crash qualifies, an emergency countdown gives you a chance to choose “I’m fine” or request help before configured alerts are sent.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_4">Set up contacts and location sharing</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_4">Add trusted emergency contacts and grant location access if you want location included with alerts. Keep your medical profile up to date for responders.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_5">Bystander guidance is available</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_5">The Bystander Guide provides clear first-aid prompts and emergency call guidance. It does not replace professional medical care.</string>
